                <pb facs="0170" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg62"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic">October 21, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received October 21.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson reports the efforts of Admiral Mello, commander of the revolting
                    squadron, for the formation of a government at Catharina and his renewed threat
                    to bombard Rio de Janeiro, founded on the <pb facs="0171" n="63" xml:id="pg63"/>
                    alleged manufacturing of torpedoes at the Government arsenal; also a rumor to
                    the effect that Rio de Janeiro will be declared under blockade.</p>
            </div>
